<cem:title lang="" subtitle="">The Memo: New Employees at the Company</cem:title>
<cem:description lang="">This virtual learning object "The Memo: New Employees at the Company" that makes part of the lesson No: 6, First Day of Work, which in turn belongs to the Upper-intermediate (B2.2) of the teaching of English as a Foreign Language, is intended to work on: write about facts about events or actions; write about hopes and expectations for the future. The grammar of this LO refers to: future continuous and future perfect, e.g. we hope that you will have organized your schedules by then so everyone can meet him; present perfect, simple past, simple present, present perfect continuous, e.g. lincoln green has accepted our offer of employment as director of advertising design. Also, the vocabulary considers: jobs, professions and careers, e.g. welcoming email, director of advertising design, liaison.</cem:description>
