<cem:description>
<cem:recommendedUse lang="en">This digital resource can be used as an activity that allows the learner to reflect on the use of grammar of English language in different communicative contexts. The instructor can work further on activities and tasks that help learners to improve their procedural knowledge.</cem:recommendedUse>
<cem:triggerQuestion lang="en">What information do you think employers should include when talking about a new employee?; What information should they not discuss? Why?</cem:triggerQuestion>
<cem:pedagogicalAspect lang="en">This learning object "The Memo: New Employees at the Company" that is part of the lesson No: 6, First Day of Work, which in turn belongs to the Upper-intermediate (B2.2) of the teaching of English as a Foreign Language, allows the learner to develop the following topics: future continuous and future perfect, e.g. we hope that you will have organized your schedules by then so everyone can meet him; present perfect, simple past, simple present, present perfect continuous, e.g. lincoln green has accepted our offer of employment as director of advertising design. It is presented within the context of write about facts about events or actions; write about hopes and expectations for the future. The student will be exposed to vocabulary related to: jobs, professions and careers, e.g. welcoming email, director of advertising design, liaison. Learners will develop their language skills by using an online content as well as the guidance of a SENA instructor.</cem:pedagogicalAspect>
<cem:learningGoal lang="en">The purpose of this learning object is to analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts.</cem:learningGoal>
</cem:description>
</cem:educational>
