<cem:description lang="en">This lesson: "First Day of Work" belongs to Upper-intermediate (B2.2). It is composed of twelve learning objects, that have the following learning outcomes: analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts; describe necessity, duty, advice, or strong dissaproval in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts; identify ways of improving aspects of communication in english based on the learning outcomes for level upper intermediate. On the other hand, the communicative functions of this lesson are: express necessity, duty, and advice; express true, untrue, and possible events in present and past; exchange opinions; request or report facts about events or actions; deal with communication breakdowns; explain how to do things; discuss hopes and expectations for the future; write about facts about events or actions; write about hopes and expectations for the future.</cem:description>
</cem:resource>
